Z||000000||Galen||09-13-2001||07:47 PM||||I took my TBI off to replace some cracked vacume lines, on my 88(87) Auto 2.5, when I did my gasket(?) I guess came off the bottom and pieces of it fell off. I put it back together and got everything hooked back up and now its not idling well at all and is giving me a code 33(map).. Could the pieces that fell off the gasket have been important? or did I just hook the vac lines back up wrong?<P><BR>edit: I forgot to add, when its in P or N, if I rev it up, when I let go of the gas it acts like its going to cut off.<P>------------------<BR>Ray -   <A HREF="mailto:galen@ezrpg.com">galen@ezrpg.com</A>    - <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank><B>Fierolinks!</B></A> - <FONT COLOR="blue">Carolina Panthers: <B>1-0-0</B></FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="purple">1988 Hawaiin Orchid Coupe</FONT> - AIM<B>:</B> Fiero88cpe - ICQ<B>:</B> 98668558<p>[This message has been edited by Galen (edited 09-13-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||Leper||09-13-2001||08:08 PM||||A new gasket is a cheap way to find out.<BR>The vac lines seemed to me like they were simple enought to put back right.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||09-13-2001||08:10 PM||||I'd about bet you MAP sensor is on the wrong port. That or it's line is broken/blocked.<P>Connect them as shown on the VECI label on the deck lid. they go from left to right on the TBI just like on the label. The 2 from the vapor canister are size coded to the corresponding TBI port.<P>make sure you didn't mess up the PCV line. Clamp all joints in that line. don't overtighten or you'll damage the rubbers.<P>You need a new mounting gasket. It's available thru any standard parts store.<P>There are three styles. The correct gasket will have 4 holes. (2 bolts, main bore, and IAC bore.) you can also use the one that has a wegde cut between the IAC and main bore. You cannot use the 3 hole one.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif">   <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 09-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Galen||09-15-2001||04:10 AM||||I swapped the vac line that was going to the egr to go to the map sensor, no more check engine light, and no more rough idle.. but she's idling up at 3k.. could this be the gasket causing a vacum leak?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Indiana_resto_guy||09-15-2001||07:47 AM||||Did you have your IAC valve out and maybe repositioned the piston?<BR>If you did, drive the car over 35 MPH for a short time and the IAC will reposition for the proper idle speed.<BR>Otherwise I'm with the rest - vac problem/leak.||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||09-15-2001||06:58 PM||||You probably have a vacuum leak. You have to replace the TBI mounting gasket.<P>The TBI ports... Left to right.<P>Vapor can, large line<BR>Vapor can, small line<BR>EGR<BR>MAP<P>You also need to reset the ECM.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif"> <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Galen||09-15-2001||11:22 PM||||I replaced the TBI gasket too.. 3.99 I figured it couldn't hurt since the old one was in rough shape. When I reset the ecm it idled back to where it should be. So all is back to the condition it was before, not saying that thats a good one but its better than it not running  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/g-flag-sig.gif"> <FONT COLOR="purple">1988 Hawaiin Orchid Coupe</FONT> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/g-flagnc-sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
